>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `del_looper`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.del_looper : string -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes a named extension looper installed by `add_looper`, `set_looper`
or `looper_ss`. Use `del_split` for split rules.

### Failure

Never fails. A missing name produces a warning and returns the input set.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.add_looper ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
     ext_bool_ss;
>>_ val without_conj = simpExtLib.del_looper "conj" ss;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.add_looper`](#simpExtLib.add_looper),
[`simpExtLib.del_split`](#simpExtLib.del_split).
